# ============================================================
# Rarefaction Curve Analysis for Bracken Reports (Shannon Index)
# Analytical (exact) version — VS Code-friendly, config at top
# ============================================================
#
# WHY THIS VERSION IS DIFFERENT FROM A SIMULATED SHANNON SCRIPT
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Standard Shannon rarefaction scripts repeatedly resample reads,
# calculate the Shannon index at each depth, and fit a log curve
# (e.g. a*log(x)+b). This introduces random sampling noise, seed
# dependence, and extrapolation bias.
#
# Because expectation is linear, the expected Shannon Index E[H(m)]
# at subsampling depth m can be computed EXACTLY in closed form:
#
#   E[H(m)] = sum_i E[ - (X_i / m) * ln(X_i / m) ]
#           = sum_i sum_{k=1}^{min(n_i, m)} [ - (k/m) * ln(k/m) * P(X_i = k) ]
#
# where X_i ~ Hypergeometric(N, n_i, m) represents the observed read count
# of taxon i when subsampling m reads from a total of N reads.
#
# This script is deterministic, exact, reproducible, and fast.
# ============================================================

